// GEORGE BOO'L'S PLATFORM-FIGHTER FACET — his values, in the repository that
// owns character-authored material.
//
//  this file MOVED here from `game/ambition_demo_smash/assets/fighters/` on
// 2026-08-19, on the 2026-08-19 GPT review's finding: *"Smash should select
// George; it should not own George's values."* The demo's own module called it
// "THIS DEMO'S CHARACTER PACKAGE", which was the wrong physical owner for
// exactly the reason this repository's README states — it owns
// "game/ruleset-specific character FACET VALUES", and the Rust repo owns the
// schema, preparation and runtime meaning those values conform to.
//
// His moves, grab and throws included, are in `smash_moveset.ron` beside this
// file, with the reasoning that justified each number. They were composed Rust
// (`george_booul_moveset.rs`) and a `capture` kit here until 2026-09-26, when
// every fighter's moves became content (fast-iteration I2, AP53): one table per
// fighter, and one home for a grab.
//
// The consuming pack is `game/ambition_demo_smash/assets/pack.ron`, which now
// SELECTS this file by relative path rather than carrying a copy of it.

// George Boo'l's platform-fighter facet — the excluded middle, as VALUES.
//
//  these numbers were Rust literals in `src/george_booul_moveset.rs` until
// D166's first facet landed. They moved verbatim, with the reasoning that
// justified them, because the reasoning is the character: a value with no reason
// beside it is the thing that gets "balanced" by somebody who does not know what
// it was for.
(
    character: "smash_george_booul",
    // ⭐ HE IS THE HEAVY, and this is where he says so.
    //
    // ⛔ this number was a `match definition.id` arm in the Smash demo's own
    // Rust until 2026-08-31 — a game-owned table writing `Vitals::knockback_
    // weight`, an ordinary character fact the engine already owns, keyed by
    // character id. `character-authoring-package.md` names that shape as a
    // falsifier in as many words, and George is the one fighter this repository
    // authors, so he is the one who stops being described from outside.
    //
    // ⭐ 1.35 IS A SPREAD, NOT AN ABSOLUTE. `scaled_knockback` DIVIDES the growth
    // term by it, so 1.35 means a launch that sends the reference body 100px
    // sends George 74. The stage is tuned against the middleweight at 1.0; his
    // whole design is that he commits and then survives the punish, and a
    // heavy that launches like everyone else has traded away his slow grab and
    // his 0.42 down-throw for nothing.
    knockback_weight: Some(1.35),
)
